  "caseId": "case15",
  "description": "The initial state of a FILE STATUS area, and the ACCTFILE half of the capability asymmetry. app/cbl/CBSTM03B.CBL:95-97 declares ACCTFILE-STATUS with no VALUE clause, so before any I/O it holds SPACES - and a plain 'R' against an ACCESS MODE IS RANDOM file matches no IF in 4000-ACCTFILE-PROC, falls into 4900-EXIT and moves that untouched value into LK-M03B-RC. The first call therefore reports two spaces, which no successful or failed operation can produce. The OPEN that follows sets '00', and the second plain read reports that stale '00' - the same no-op, now over a status that has been written once.",
